{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KYhYED3W8q3zctNURXsB5U","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"better-sqlite3 12 backup method async promise API\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"better-sqlite3/docs/api.md at master · WiseLibs/better-sqlite3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/WiseLibs/better-sqlite3/blob/master/docs/api.md\"},{\"title\":\"better-sqlite3/docs/api.md at 03f382a3ba1977feeb57ff1349c628b846d8b8b3 · WiseLibs/better-sqlite3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/WiseLibs/better-sqlite3/blob/03f382a3ba1977feeb57ff1349c628b846d8b8b3/docs/api.md\"},{\"title\":\"Async API? · Issue #89 · WiseLibs/better-sqlite3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JoshuaWise/better-sqlite3/issues/89\"},{\"title\":\"better-sqlite3 - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/better-sqlite3\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - fhellwig/sqlite-async: ES6 Promise-based interface to the sqlite3 module.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/fhellwig/sqlite-async\"},{\"title\":\"Top 5 better-sqlite3 Code Examples | Snyk\",\"url\":\"https://snyk.io/advisor/npm-package/better-sqlite3/example\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tguichaoua/promised-sqlite3: A wrapper for sqlite3 node.js package to use Promise.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tguichaoua/promised-sqlite3\"},{\"title\":\"sqlite-async - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/sqlite-async\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding Better-SQLite3: The Fastest SQLite Library for Node.js - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/lovestaco/understanding-better-sqlite3-the-fastest-sqlite-library-for-nodejs-4n8\"},{\"title\":\"Workers and Promises (a.k.a. Worker1 and Promiser)\",\"url\":\"https://sqlite.org/wasm/doc/trunk/api-worker1.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the better-sqlite3 backup method with async promise API:\n\n## better-sqlite3 Backup Method\n\nThe `.backup()` method in better-sqlite3 initiates a backup of the database, returning a promise for when the backup is complete. If the backup fails, the promise will be rejected with an Error.\n\n### Key Features:\n\n- You can optionally backup an attached database instead by setting the `attached` option to the name of the desired attached database.\n- A backup file is just a regular SQLite database file. It can be opened by `new Database()` just like any SQLite database.\n\n### Usage Example:\n\n```javascript\ndb.backup(`backup-${Date.now()}.db`)\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('backup complete!');\n  })\n  .catch((err) => {\n    console.log('backup failed:', err);\n  });\n```\n\nYou can continue to use the database normally while a backup is in progress. If the same database connection mutates the database while performing a backup, those mutations will be reflected in the backup automatically.\n\n### Progress Callback:\n\nIf the backup is successful, the returned promise will contain an object that has the same properties as the one provided to the progress callback, but `.remainingPages` will be 0. If the progress callback throws an exception, the backup will be aborted. Usually this happens due to an unexpected error, but you can also use this behavior to voluntarily cancel the backup operation. If the parent database connection is closed, all pending backups will be automatically aborted.\n\n### Important Note on Transactions:\n\nTransaction functions do not work with async functions. Technically speaking, async functions always return after the first await, which means the transaction will already be committed before any async code executes. Also, because SQLite serializes all transactions, it's generally a very bad idea to keep a transaction open across event loop ticks anyways.\n\n### Why Synchronous API for Most Operations:\n\nbetter-sqlite3 provides an \"Easy-to-use synchronous API (better concurrency than an asynchronous API).\"(no content)node-sqlite3 uses asynchronous APIs for serialized operations — which actually hurts performance. better-sqlite3 executes everything synchronously, avoiding event loop complexity and improving concurrency.\n\nThe backup method is one of the few asynchronous/promise-based APIs in better-sqlite3, as it makes sense for long-running backup operations to be non-blocking.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"130e55cd-d481-4dd7-b33f-e0bdbfb691b6","uuid":"81f11005-ba6b-4e93-9d8f-9b07d42504f8","tool_use_result":{"query":"better-sqlite3 12 backup method async promise API","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013vzrmkyL6sBMGeCTB4FY23","content":[{"title":"better-sqlite3/docs/api.md at master · WiseLibs/better-sqlite3","url":"https://github.com/WiseLibs/better-sqlite3/blob/master/docs/api.md"},{"title":"better-sqlite3/docs/api.md at 03f382a3ba1977feeb57ff1349c628b846d8b8b3 · WiseLibs/better-sqlite3","url":"https://github.com/WiseLibs/better-sqlite3/blob/03f382a3ba1977feeb57ff1349c628b846d8b8b3/docs/api.md"},{"title":"Async API? · Issue #89 · WiseLibs/better-sqlite3","url":"https://github.com/JoshuaWise/better-sqlite3/issues/89"},{"title":"better-sqlite3 - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/better-sqlite3"},{"title":"GitHub - fhellwig/sqlite-async: ES6 Promise-based interface to the sqlite3 module.","url":"https://github.com/fhellwig/sqlite-async"},{"title":"Top 5 better-sqlite3 Code Examples | Snyk","url":"https://snyk.io/advisor/npm-package/better-sqlite3/example"},{"title":"GitHub - tguichaoua/promised-sqlite3: A wrapper for sqlite3 node.js package to use Promise.","url":"https://github.com/tguichaoua/promised-sqlite3"},{"title":"sqlite-async - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/sqlite-async"},{"title":"Understanding Better-SQLite3: The Fastest SQLite Library for Node.js - DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/lovestaco/understanding-better-sqlite3-the-fastest-sqlite-library-for-nodejs-4n8"},{"title":"Workers and Promises (a.k.a. Worker1 and Promiser)","url":"https://sqlite.org/wasm/doc/trunk/api-worker1.md"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the better-sqlite3 backup method with async promise API:\n\n## better-sqlite3 Backup Method\n\nThe `.backup()` method in better-sqlite3 initiates a backup of the database, returning a promise for when the backup is complete. If the backup fails, the promise will be rejected with an Error.\n\n### Key Features:\n\n- You can optionally backup an attached database instead by setting the `attached` option to the name of the desired attached database.\n- A backup file is just a regular SQLite database file. It can be opened by `new Database()` just like any SQLite database.\n\n### Usage Example:\n\n```javascript\ndb.backup(`backup-${Date.now()}.db`)\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('backup complete!');\n  })\n  .catch((err) => {\n    console.log('backup failed:', err);\n  });\n```\n\nYou can continue to use the database normally while a backup is in progress. If the same database connection mutates the database while performing a backup, those mutations will be reflected in the backup automatically.\n\n### Progress Callback:\n\nIf the backup is successful, the returned promise will contain an object that has the same properties as the one provided to the progress callback, but `.remainingPages` will be 0. If the progress callback throws an exception, the backup will be aborted. Usually this happens due to an unexpected error, but you can also use this behavior to voluntarily cancel the backup operation. If the parent database connection is closed, all pending backups will be automatically aborted.\n\n### Important Note on Transactions:\n\nTransaction functions do not work with async functions. Technically speaking, async functions always return after the first await, which means the transaction will already be committed before any async code executes. Also, because SQLite serializes all transactions, it's generally a very bad idea to keep a transaction open across event loop ticks anyways.\n\n### Why Synchronous API for Most Operations:\n\nbetter-sqlite3 provides an \"Easy-to-use synchronous API (better concurrency than an asynchronous API).\"(no content)node-sqlite3 uses asynchronous APIs for serialized operations — which actually hurts performance. better-sqlite3 executes everything synchronously, avoiding event loop complexity and improving concurrency.\n\nThe backup method is one of the few asynchronous/promise-based APIs in better-sqlite3, as it makes sense for long-running backup operations to be non-blocking."],"durationSeconds":17.10252854099999}}
