{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T3nyaoT8M1gZtpof2qPEF5","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/progress.txt has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"130e55cd-d481-4dd7-b33f-e0bdbfb691b6","uuid":"653462a1-0fd6-4747-95d9-2de85a3a55f0","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/samueledwards/RalphWiggumV3/progress.txt","oldString":"---\n[2026-01-16] US-001 - Dashboard builds without errors\n- What was implemented: Verified dashboard build process\n- Files checked: dashboard package.json, TypeScript config\n- **Learnings:**\n  - npm install shows 7 moderate vulnerabilities but doesn't block builds\n  - tsc --noEmit passes cleanly with no TypeScript errors\n  - Vite build produces ~500KB JS bundle (143KB gzipped)\n---","newString":"---\n[2026-01-16] US-001 - Dashboard builds without errors\n- What was implemented: Verified dashboard build process\n- Files checked: dashboard package.json, TypeScript config\n- **Learnings:**\n  - npm install shows 7 moderate vulnerabilities but doesn't block builds\n  - tsc --noEmit passes cleanly with no TypeScript errors\n  - Vite build produces ~500KB JS bundle (143KB gzipped)\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] US-002 - Backend server starts and accepts WebSocket connections\n- What was implemented: Fixed async/sync bug in database backup system\n- Files changed: dashboard/server/database/backup.ts, dashboard/server/healthMonitor.ts\n- **Learnings:**\n  - better-sqlite3 db.backup() returns a Promise - must await before accessing the backup file\n  - Server logs \"Ralph Dashboard server started\" with port info (not \"Server running on port\")\n  - HealthMonitor calls DatabaseBackup.performDailyBackupIfNeeded() on startup\n  - Pattern: Don't block startup on async operations - use .catch() for error handling\n---","originalFile":"# Progress Log\n\nThis file tracks learnings, patterns, and discoveries across Ralph Wiggum iterations.\nEntries are append-only - never delete, only add.\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] Simple Mode Verification Started\n- Goal: Verify Ralph Wiggum V3 dashboard is complete and functional\n- Mode: Simple (using prd.json for task tracking)\n- Key files: prd.json (tasks), progress.txt (learnings), .ralph-mode (workflow mode)\n- Dashboard location: ./dashboard\n- Build: cd dashboard && npm run build\n- Typecheck: cd dashboard && npx tsc --noEmit\n- Dev server: cd dashboard && npm run dev (port 5173)\n- Backend: cd dashboard && npx tsx server/index.ts (port 3001)\n- Pattern: Check TypeScript compiles BEFORE marking story complete\n- Pattern: Run the actual commands to verify, don't just check file existence\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-16] US-001 - Dashboard builds without errors\n- What was implemented: Verified dashboard build process\n- Files checked: dashboard package.json, TypeScript config\n- **Learnings:**\n  - npm install shows 7 moderate vulnerabilities but doesn't block builds\n  - tsc --noEmit passes cleanly with no TypeScript errors\n  - Vite build produces ~500KB JS bundle (143KB gzipped)\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-15] Project Initialized\n- Pattern: Created complete Ralph Wiggum documentation suite\n- Tip: Start with AUDIENCE_JTBD.md to ground all specs in user needs\n- Tip: Use SLC releases to ship value incrementally\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-15] Agent Installation Feature Set Complete\n- Pattern: Most features in Releases 1-3 were already implemented, needed systematic verification\n- Pattern: Agent installation follows the established WebSocket message pattern: add type, handler, state, UI\n- Gotcha: The dashboard's npm run typecheck script doesn't exist - use `npx tsc --noEmit` instead\n- Gotcha: Pre-existing lint errors in the codebase (unused vars, case block declarations) - not blockers\n- Tip: YAML frontmatter in agent .md files enables name/description parsing for the UI\n- Tip: No git remote configured - push will need `git remote add origin <url>` first\n---\n\n---\n[2026-01-15] Documentation Sync Complete\n- Pattern: Keep tasks.json in sync with IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md when tasks are completed\n- Pattern: Include all 5 releases (10 Feature Sets) in documentation for completeness\n- Gotcha: tasks.json was outdated (showing 31 pending tasks) while IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md showed 63 complete\n- Tip: Always verify both tracking files match before signaling ALL_TASKS_COMPLETE\n- Tip: Git tags should reflect major milestones (v0.0.4 for Feature Set 10, v0.0.5 for doc sync)\n---\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":28,"oldLines":6,"newStart":28,"newLines":17,"lines":[" ---"," "," ---","+[2026-01-16] US-002 - Backend server starts and accepts WebSocket connections","+- What was implemented: Fixed async/sync bug in database backup system","+- Files changed: dashboard/server/database/backup.ts, dashboard/server/healthMonitor.ts","+- **Learnings:**","+  - better-sqlite3 db.backup() returns a Promise - must await before accessing the backup file","+  - Server logs \"Ralph Dashboard server started\" with port info (not \"Server running on port\")","+  - HealthMonitor calls DatabaseBackup.performDailyBackupIfNeeded() on startup","+  - Pattern: Don't block startup on async operations - use .catch() for error handling","+---","+","+---"," [2026-01-15] Project Initialized"," - Pattern: Created complete Ralph Wiggum documentation suite"," - Tip: Start with AUDIENCE_JTBD.md to ground all specs in user needs"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
